    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d160">

                <pb facs="0499" n="477" sameAs="frus:frus1946v02/pg477"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">884.014/5–1346</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ethiopian Prime
                        Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Endalkachen</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-06-05">June 5, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of April 4, 1946, regarding Ethiopia’s claims to Eritrea
                    and Italian Somaliland.<anchor n="35a" xml:id="d160-f1"/></p>
                <p>I know that I need not assure Your Excellency of the high regard in which the
                    American people hold the people of Ethiopia and of their recognition of the
                    magnificent struggle which so happily resulted in the re-emergence of an
                    independent Ethiopia. It has also been the constant wish of this Government to
                    give every encouragement which it properly could to the unfettered development
                    of your country.</p>
                <p>In keeping with the friendship and close association which have so long existed
                    between our two Peoples and Government, I assure you that Ethiopia’s position on
                    the question of the disposition of Eritrea and Italian Somaliland will be given
                    every possible consideration by this Government.</p>
                <p>Accept, Excellency, the assurances of my most distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer>[<signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James</hi> F. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d160-f1" n="35a" xml:id="d160-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; in it the Ethiopian Prime Minister asked the United States to assert
                    its leadership in order to assure the return of Eritrea and Somaliland to
                    Ethiopia. The Prime Minister’s communication was delivered to the Department of
                    State under cover of a note of May 13, 1946, also not printed
                    (884.014/5–1346).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
